        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ec5a420f-8228-5ecf-b70a-2eda2ff9793e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Gilgit-Baltistan, Pakistan, China\n- Mountains: Trivor, The Crown, Crown Peak, Huang Guan Shan, Huangguan Shan, Momhil Sar, Yengisogat\n- Mountain ranges: Karakoram, Hispar Muztagh\n\nFacts:\n- Trivor is one of the high peaks of the Hispar Muztagh subrange of the Karakoram range in Gilgit-Baltistan, Pakistan.\n- The Crown is also known as Huang Guan Shan and sometimes Crown Peak, and it is a mountain in the Karakoram range in China.\n- Momhil Sar is situated in the Hispar Muztagh subrange of the Karakoram range a few kilometres northwest of its parent peak Trivor.\n- Yengisogat's highest peak is Huangguan Shan, or Crown Peak, with a height of 7,265 m (23,835 ft), though it is sometimes given as 7,295 m (23,934 ft).",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
